/3 that's like dividing by 3  24 divided by 3 is 8 okay let's look at  letter K 70% of 40 let's find 10% that's  4 7 times 4 is 28 15 percent now this  one we can do a couple different ways 15  percent is really like 10 percent plus 5  percent let's find out what 10 percent  is 10 percent we move that one place to  the left that's going to be 2.8 now 5  percent is half of 10 percent right so  half of 2.8 is 1.4 if we add those  together you can see we're getting 4.2  okay so that's a good way to do it 10  percent cut the 10% and 1/2 add them  together 50 percent we talked about was  half so half of 90 is 45 75 percent  let's find out what 25 percent is that's  like dividing by 4 that's like 1/4 so  that's going to be 4 and 75 percent is 3  times 25% so 3 times 4 is 12  250% now this is a more challenging one  see 100 percent really means the whole  thing right if somebody says I'm gonna  give you 100 percent you know of my  sandwich that's the whole thing right  but 200 percent would be like 2 times as  much 250% 50 percents like half so we're  really talking about two and a half  times as much so let's do two times as  much 2 times 38 is 76 half of 38 is 19  if we add those together what do we get  5:1 we're looking at 95 okay so the last  one 66 and 2/3 percent we're talking  about 2/3 but let's talk about 1/3  that's 33 and 1/3 percent 1/3 when you  divide by 3 that's 1/3 so that's going  to be 9 66 and 2/3 is double 33 and 1/3  so if we multiply this by 2 you can see  we're getting 18 so that's the basic  idea if you understand this idea of one  percent moving the decimal one place to  the left I'm sorry two places to left 10  percent you're just moving at one place  to the left 33 and a third is dividing  by 3 25% is dividing by 4 50 percent is  dividing in half 66 and 2/3 is double 33  one third so figure out this first and  then double those are the key ones if  you understand those it'll be easy to  calculate these percentages mentally so  I hope that helped